                "Two yardsticks. **P/E** compares the share price with profit after tax. **EV/EBITDA** compares the value of the whole business (market value plus debt, minus cash) with operating profit, so it gives credit for cash and charges for debt. In this sector the two disagree for two reasons: a few companies hold large treasuries whose interest lifts profit (Avanti, KRBL, Kaveri), and a few have borrowed heavily to buy or build (Zydus, Hindustan Foods).",
